 "notes": [
  "All block edges and expiry dates come from UKE's national reservation pages and the UKE list of national reservations (19 Feb 2026 xlsx). The seed (davwheat) matched UKE for 700/900/2100/2600/3600.",
  "UKE's 'unified expiry' policy targets: 700/800 MHz 31 May 2040, 900 MHz 31 Dec 2038, 1800/2100 MHz 31 Dec 2037, 2600 MHz 31 Dec 2039, 3600 MHz 30 Nov 2038. Several current reservations still carry earlier dates (e.g. 800 MHz 2031, 1800 MHz 2027/2029); the block-level expiry fields show the dates on the UKE list.",
  "Totals: Plus 2x30 MHz of 1800 is the largest 1800 holding; Plus also holds 2x2.5 MHz at 420 MHz (group 450). PGE Systemy's LTE450 network is a private utility network.",
  "Orange and T-Mobile share their radio networks through the NetWorkS! joint venture; this is noted from background knowledge (not verified in this pass)."
 ],
